<div class="page-title">🔒 <span class="page-title-text">End-User Evaluation — Informed Consent</span></div>
<p class="page-subtitle">Before anything is recorded, please read this and choose whether to take part. Participation is entirely voluntary and has no effect on your use of CMA-Flow either way.</p>

<div class="form-card wide" style="margin-bottom: 22px;">
  <div class="form-title" style="font-size: 18px;">What this evaluation is</div>
  <p class="form-hint" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">
    This is a short usability evaluation of CMA-Flow's six analytics modules (Upload, Browse, Descriptive,
    Diagnostic, Predictive, Prescriptive), conducted by Brenda M. Balala, a Doctor of Information Technology
    candidate at AMA University, as part of her dissertation research. It is separate from your normal use of
    CMA-Flow and from any monetization configuration or dataset you manage in the app.
  </p>

  <div class="form-title" style="font-size: 15px; margin-top: 18px;">What would be collected</div>
  <p class="form-hint" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">If you agree to participate, this evaluation records:</p>
  <ul style="margin: 0 0 6px; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-muted);">
    <li>A log of the six walkthrough tasks: whether each was completed, time spent, whether you needed
      assistance, whether you hit an error, and any optional notes you choose to add.</li>
    <li>Your ratings and optional remarks on the 17-item questionnaire about your experience.</li>
    <li>Your account identifier and business name, used only to let you resume where you left off and for the
      researcher to review evaluation progress — never published or shared outside this research.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="form-hint" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
    No new personal information is requested beyond what your CMA-Flow account already has. This evaluation
    does not touch your uploaded datasets or monetization configurations.
  </p>

  <div class="form-title" style="font-size: 15px; margin-top: 18px;">How it would be used</div>
  <p class="form-hint" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
    Responses are analyzed and reported only in aggregate and de-identified form (for example, average ratings
    across all respondents) in the researcher's dissertation and any related academic publication. Individual
    responses are not identified by name or account in any report, and are retained only for the duration of
    this research and its reporting.
  </p>

  <div class="form-title" style="font-size: 15px; margin-top: 18px;">Your rights under the Data Privacy Act (Republic Act No. 10173)</div>
  <p class="form-hint" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">As a data subject, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul style="margin: 0 0 6px; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-muted);">
    <li>Decline to participate, with no penalty and no effect on your access to CMA-Flow.</li>
    <li>Withdraw your consent at any time, even after starting — a "Withdraw from this evaluation" link is
      available throughout, and anything not yet completed is simply excluded from reporting.</li>
    <li>Be informed of, access, and request correction or erasure of your responses.</li>
    <li>Object to further processing, and lodge a complaint with the National Privacy Commission.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="form-hint" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
    To exercise any of these rights, or ask a question about this evaluation, contact the researcher at
    <a href="mailto:bmbalala@ndmu.edu.ph">bmbalala@ndmu.edu.ph</a>.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="form-card wide" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <form method="POST" action="/evaluation/consent">
    <input type="hidden" name="decision" value="agree" />
    <label class="field-checkbox" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
      <input type="checkbox" id="consent-ack" required />
      I have read and understood the information above, and I voluntarily agree to participate.
    </label>
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-accent" id="consent-agree-btn">I Agree — Start the Evaluation →</button>
  </form>
</div>

<div class="form-card wide">
  <p class="form-hint" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
    Prefer not to take part? That's completely fine — you can still use every other part of CMA-Flow as usual.
  </p>
  <form method="POST" action="/evaluation/consent">
    <input type="hidden" name="decision" value="decline" />
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-ghost">I Do Not Wish to Participate</button>
  </form>
</div>
